  "Formed from the 1989 merger of Novo Terapeutisk Laboratorium and Nordisk Insulinlaboratorium, both founded in the early 1920s to produce insulin in Denmark. Headquartered in Bagsværd and controlled by the Novo Nordisk Foundation. Mike Doustdar became CEO in 2025. Products: Ozempic and Rybelsus for type 2 diabetes, Wegovy for obesity — all semaglutide — plus a large insulin portfolio and rare disease treatments in haemophilia. Novo lost significant ground to Lilly through 2025 and 2026 as tirzepatide outperformed semaglutide on weight loss.",
